        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                "word": "pérégrination",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "addbe746-c54a-4276-95fd-82fb7b7a27a7",
                        "entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pérégrinations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fdcddf26-3efb-36d6-8a52-35b002f0b0ee",
                        "entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Voyage fait dans des pays éloignés."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19429fc2-b9f9-461f-9ac7-f17467a53778",
                                "sense_id": "fdcddf26-3efb-36d6-8a52-35b002f0b0ee",
                                "text": "Lacan, qui sait conduire une horde, menace ceux qui seraient tentés par le départ : si vous m’abandonnez, vous deviendrez des pourceaux, leur dit-il en rappelant comment les compagnons d’Ulysse, las de suivre leur capitaine dans une pérégrination qui leur paraissait sans fin, s’étaient laissé ensorceler par Circé."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbb09a3b-1f90-3c37-9425-5a2029412b86",
                        "entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Voyage volontaire, associé à la difficulté et à la pauvreté dans la tradition chrétienne."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fa547f3-7cd1-4e02-90fb-0b7c06d0ace0",
                                "sense_id": "bbb09a3b-1f90-3c37-9425-5a2029412b86",
                                "text": "Les uns la présentent comme agréable : peregrinatio voluptuaria ; ce cas est rare : nous dirions aujourd'hui qu'il s'agit d'un voyage touristique. Plus souvent le contexte montre que la pérégrination est considérée comme pénible : labores peregrinationis, labores peregrinationis, peregrinationis incommoda ou suspiria... Généralement on est privé encore d'autre chose que des amitiés, qui sont les richesses de l'âme ; on est privé de tout, en tout cas de tout ce qui est commode : la pérégrination est une forme de pauvreté."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f16eac8-7b25-3d93-ad11-6954fe83f422",
                        "entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Série de déplacements, d’allées et venues, de voyages multiples et compliqués."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ad5951f-52d0-400b-81b0-577b5d1da4c2",
                                "sense_id": "2f16eac8-7b25-3d93-ad11-6954fe83f422",
                                "text": "Paulina Barnett fit le récit de ses propres pérégrinations à travers les contrées intertropicales."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "611c8edd-b8ca-48e6-9fb2-f3a067d313e3",
                                "sense_id": "2f16eac8-7b25-3d93-ad11-6954fe83f422",
                                "text": "Le cheval qui est le compagnon fidèle de l’homme est aussi capable de le suivre dans toutes ses pérégrinations […] Comme son maître, il est cosmopolite […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da3e87d0-872b-4c03-9f46-ec5abe7d3802",
                                "sense_id": "2f16eac8-7b25-3d93-ad11-6954fe83f422",
                                "text": "Je suis à Bakou, j’ai une demi-journée pour visiter Bakou, et je n’en perdrai pas une heure, puisque les hasards de mes pérégrinations m’ont conduit à Bakou."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56743566-719a-4e3d-abed-e4c99b165413",
                                "sense_id": "2f16eac8-7b25-3d93-ad11-6954fe83f422",
                                "text": "Salt mort, il fallut déménager. Alors commença cette longue pérégrination d’appartement en appartement qui est un des côtés les plus odieux de la vie citadine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "392ba7a0-db00-4a77-b109-d07c209816b5",
                                "sense_id": "2f16eac8-7b25-3d93-ad11-6954fe83f422",
                                "text": "En général, les leffs concernent des familles et non des territoires et l'appartenance à un leff résiste à la pérégrination."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d924af67-f26c-4f63-8149-67cd6686c937",
                        "source_entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "target_lang_word": "pelgrimstocht",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pelgrimstocht",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55f096e3-d1a5-31ca-a1a2-308fff258e3e",
                                        "entry_id": "1fae5236-f8bb-342b-88ec-7e7233b72936",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "de bedevaart"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4e71a5a-1a9e-4b6c-9c20-2fde31d1ea1f",
                                                "sense_id": "55f096e3-d1a5-31ca-a1a2-308fff258e3e",
                                                "text": "De pelgrimstocht naar Mekka verliep normaal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a262564f-cb46-4106-a301-4e0b52d4cfac",
                                                "sense_id": "55f096e3-d1a5-31ca-a1a2-308fff258e3e",
                                                "text": "Jaren later liep ik op mijn 42ste de 88 Tempels Trail, een pelgrimstocht van 1.300 kilometer door Japan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11625256-8aea-4083-a73d-e9b9da363058",
                                                "sense_id": "55f096e3-d1a5-31ca-a1a2-308fff258e3e",
                                                "text": "In de pelgrimstochten die ik in het verleden heb gelopen, de boeddhistische 88 Tempels tocht in Japan en de katholieke Camino de Santiago in Spanje, speelt het geloof een belangrijke rol."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f037accb-3d94-4eec-aa8c-07e68fac7207",
                        "source_entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "target_lang_word": "omzwerving",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "omzwerving",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1b303082-7c5b-365c-8701-c7d9cf7d5924",
                                        "entry_id": "3a1b392b-8cd7-3680-bac9-2c9c7c836b0e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "het omzwerven; het steeds op een andere plaats verbijven"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "434872f8-836e-474e-b1a9-a68b7301208f",
                                                "sense_id": "1b303082-7c5b-365c-8701-c7d9cf7d5924",
                                                "text": "List woonde vanaf haar zevende jaar, na omzwervingen in weeshuizen, bij Jaap en Marie List op Vlieland. Uiteindelijk nam ze ook hun achternaam aan. Tot haar achttiende verbleef ze op het Waddeneiland, om vervolgens haar geluk te beproeven in Amsterdam, waar ze tot aan haar overlijden op 78-jarige leeftijd woonde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e828e990-6933-4499-af8a-d12595b464b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "5764432d-a6bd-3b01-bdc0-c7d2614a85e2",
                        "target_lang_word": "peregrination",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "peregrination",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b699cf35-54f6-3420-9973-914b4155ca2b",
                                        "entry_id": "104c25e3-6bdd-3182-9f72-3a51b56697f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person's life regarded as a temporary stay on earth and a journey to the afterlife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12c58e2a-a873-40fe-a5b9-2c1594fb7e66",
                                                "sense_id": "b699cf35-54f6-3420-9973-914b4155ca2b",
                                                "text": "It is true our life in this vvorld is not called a baniſhment any vvhere in the Scripture: but a pilgrimage, a peregrination, a travell; but perigrinatio cum ignominia conjunctu, exilium; he that leaves his Countrey becauſe he vvas aſhamed, or afraid to return to it, or to ſtay in it, is a baniſhed man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2dbc188-6893-3920-b1bd-8b66f046b2be",
                                        "entry_id": "104c25e3-6bdd-3182-9f72-3a51b56697f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A journey made by a pilgrim; a pilgrimage; also (uncountable) the making of pilgrimages."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2e7b438-7fbe-41ec-b081-c611ff5458d8",
                                                "sense_id": "d2dbc188-6893-3920-b1bd-8b66f046b2be",
                                                "text": "According to the mode of that time, he [Cnut the Great] made a pilgrimage to Rome, with a view to expiate the crimes, which paved his way to the throne; but he made a good use of this peregrination, and returned full of the observations he had made in the country, through which he had passed, which he turned to the benefit of his extensive dominions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                        "entry_id": "104c25e3-6bdd-3182-9f72-3a51b56697f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A journey or trip, especially by foot; also (uncountable) journeying, travelling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ccf5f1e1-e675-4574-9ad0-98704f4bc813",
                                                "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                                "text": "By what I have touch’d in the Chapter of the Elms, concerning the peregrination of that Tree into Spain (where even in Plinie’s time there were none, and where now they are in great abundance) why ſhould we not more generally endeavour to propagate the Ilex amongſt us; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f8e5baa-f87d-4777-a7b1-489f8ec231c8",
                                                "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                                "text": "[O]ur linguist having received such extraordinary rudiments towards a good education, was afterwards trained up in every thing that becomes a gentleman; wearing off by little and little all the vicious habits and practices that he had been used to in the course of his peregrinations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49a8b8e2-1787-4798-ac02-ccfbf03a83f8",
                                                "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                                "text": "[T]hey had made what might be received as one or two tolerable jests on the subject before they had advanced far on their peregrination."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fb27fae-df1c-4886-ad90-097622475954",
                                                "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                                "text": "Thus it has been my hap, in my peregrinations about this great metropolis, to blunder upon a scene which unfolded to me some of the mysteries of the book making craft, and at once put my astonishment on this head at an end."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b7626d6-3674-44b7-bcd3-bdfea796a9fc",
                                                "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                                "text": "Whence, disappearing from the constellation of the Northern Crown he would somehow reappear reborn above delta in the constellation of Cassiopeia and after incalculable eons of peregrination return an estranged avenger, a wreaker of justice on malefactors, a dark crusader, a sleeper awakened, with financial resources (by supposition) surpassing those of Rothschild or the silver king."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4854553-48ae-402d-90b6-8914e2833f03",
                                                "sense_id": "d5c89357-8fd2-3cf6-b426-f61076b74390",
                                                "text": "I suppose that nowadays the red-faced farmers, whose invariable topic (so a friendly guard who understood Welsh told me) was sheep and their prices, find their own cars or the buses more convenient than a Western Region main line for their short-distance peregrinations to market."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae100bf2-faad-3434-8e80-63e6a9a4c6ad",
                                        "entry_id": "104c25e3-6bdd-3182-9f72-3a51b56697f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Broad or systematic discussion of a subject; (countable) an instance of this; a discourse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf0128fe-7db9-3713-a643-7b748e4cc5c5",
                                        "entry_id": "104c25e3-6bdd-3182-9f72-3a51b56697f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Straying from the main subject in speech or writing; digression; (countable) an instance of this."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7f2e97d-8ccc-3202-bdd7-71f046517d22",
